<p>Last week, I asked philosophy instructors to let us know <a href="https://dailynous.com/2026/02/09/how-much-reading-do-you-assign/">how much reading they assign</a> in their undergraduate courses.<span id="more-56570"></span></p>
<p>As of yesterday afternoon, there were around 700 responses for the &#8220;lower level&#8221; philosophy course poll and a little less than that for the &#8220;upper level&#8221; philosophy course poll.</p>
<p>For lower-level philosophy courses, a little over 36% of respondents said they assigned around 20 pages of reading per week, followed by almost 21% assigning around 30 pages per week and around 18% assigning around 10 pages of reading per week.</p>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-56571" src="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/reading-assigned-poll-lower-level-2026-2.png" alt="" width="1617" height="835" srcset="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/reading-assigned-poll-lower-level-2026-2.png 1617w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/reading-assigned-poll-lower-level-2026-2-300x155.png 300w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/reading-assigned-poll-lower-level-2026-2-1024x529.png 1024w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/reading-assigned-poll-lower-level-2026-2-768x397.png 768w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/reading-assigned-poll-lower-level-2026-2-1536x793.png 1536w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/reading-assigned-poll-lower-level-2026-2-400x207.png 400w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1617px) 100vw, 1617px" /></p>
<p>For upper-level philosophy courses, around 23% percent of respondents said they assigned 30 pages of reading per week, closely followed by 22% assigning 40 pages per week. 17% say they assign around 20 pages of reading per week, and almost 16% report assigning 50 pages per week.</p>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-56572" src="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/reading-assigned-poll-upper-level-2026-2.png" alt="" width="1647" height="854" srcset="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/reading-assigned-poll-upper-level-2026-2.png 1647w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/reading-assigned-poll-upper-level-2026-2-300x156.png 300w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/reading-assigned-poll-upper-level-2026-2-1024x531.png 1024w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/reading-assigned-poll-upper-level-2026-2-768x398.png 768w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/reading-assigned-poll-upper-level-2026-2-1536x796.png 1536w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/reading-assigned-poll-upper-level-2026-2-400x207.png 400w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1647px) 100vw, 1647px" /></p>
<p>If we treat &#8220;100 or more pages&#8221; as 100 pages, the average number of pages of assigned reading per week in a lower level undergraduate philosophy course is around 27 pages, while the average in an upper level undergraduate philosophy course is around 40 pages per week.</p>
<p>Now whether the students are actually doing the assigned reading is another story.</p><p>The post <a href="https://dailynous.com/2026/02/16/how-much-reading-do-you-assign-poll-results/">How Much Reading Do You Assign? Poll Results</a> first appeared on <a href="https://dailynous.com">Daily Nous</a>.</p>